  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "DSH Plugin Manager",
      "text": "<div align=\"right\">\n\n[English](README.md) · [中文](README.zh.md)\n\n</div>\n\nAn independently publishable DSH bundle that adds a categorized plugin manager to **Settings → Plugins**.\n\nThis repository is intentionally shaped like a normal DSH community plugin:"
    },
    {
      "section": "DSH Plugin Manager",
      "text": "- the root `package.json` is the installable npm package;\n- `dsh.bundle.patch` mounts the Host gateway;\n- `dsh.client` loads the browser Settings tab in native Web clients;\n- `lib/` contains the already-built Host and Client artifacts;\n- GitHub is the source, documentation, and `dsh-plugin` market-discovery page;\n- npm is the normal installation and update channel."
    },
    {
      "section": "What it provides",
      "text": "- categories for every installed profile package;\n- GitHub `dsh-plugin` market search;\n- duplicate-install detection;\n- npm-first installation when a market repository publishes a DSH bundle;\n- GitHub fallback for unpublished repositories;\n- uninstall, single-package update, update checking, and startup checks;\n- GitHub Release checks for source-installed plugins with semver tags, with commit-head fallback for unpinned sources;\n- explicit pnpm build approval/retry with captured diagnostics;\n- an install-complete restart prompt for Desktop and native Web;\n- the same active-profile behavior in DSH Desktop and `npx @deepseek-ai/dsh web`."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install after publishing",
      "text": "Replace the package name below if the publisher renames it:\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin --profile desktop add dsh-plugin-manager-community@latest"
    },
    {
      "section": "Native Web profile",
      "text": "npx -y @deepseek-ai/dsh plugin --profile web add dsh-plugin-manager-community@latest\nnpx -y @deepseek-ai/dsh web\n```\n\nAfter installing a newer package version, restart the current DSH process so the new bundle layer is loaded. The Settings tab asks about restarting after a successful market install."
    },
    {
      "section": "Native Web profile",
      "text": "The native Web restart intentionally replaces the running Node process. Depending on browser timing, the HTTP request that triggered the restart can still surface as `Failed to fetch`; the current `lib/client.js` recognizes that Web-only disconnect as an expected restart and displays a reconnecting status. Publish `lib/index.js` and `lib/client.js` from the same release."
    },
    {
      "section": "Compatibility",
      "text": "The plugin manager is verified against **DeepSeek Harness (DSH) Desktop** and the native Web profile of the same application. The `dsh.client.platform: \"web\"` declaration describes the browser face; it is not a GitHub-only installation mode. A remote browser still controls the Host/profile running the DSH process, so package operations occur on that machine."
    },
    {
      "section": "Compatibility",
      "text": "On Windows native Web, the Host resolves pnpm in this order: `DSH_PNPM_BIN`, the active profile/shared DSH pnpm package, `PNPM_HOME`/npm global directories, PATH, and finally Node.js Corepack. Direct `.exe`/pnpm-script launches avoid shell splitting of paths such as `C:\\\\Program Files`; `.cmd` shims are quoted when needed. Command output uses UTF-8 with a GB18030 fallback so Chinese `cmd.exe` diagnostics remain readable. If none of those locations is available, install Node.js/Corepack or set `DSH_PNPM_BIN` to the full `pnpm.cmd` path, then restart the Web process."
    },
    {
      "section": "Development note",
      "text": "`lib/` is the release artifact copied from the verified Harness build. `src/` is included for review and future maintenance. The current source mirror is kept aligned with the Harness implementation; the handoff instructions publish the verified artifact directly and do not require a Harness monorepo checkout.\n\nSee [`HANDOFF.md`](HANDOFF.md) and [`PUBLISH.md`](PUBLISH.md) for the exact publishing checklist."
    }
  ],
